{"id":"20260829T003810.937264732Z-47c6aaad","time":"2026-08-29T00:38:10.937264732Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  A candidate is confined to the files its plan names: after the worker's diff is read and before validation, audit, review or admission, every changed path -- added, modified, deleted or renamed -- must be one the plan named; any other path refuses the candidate, and no test-edit grant enlarges the named set.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended with an externally supplied plan; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] runCandidate refuses a read-only plan whose candidate changed files immediately before emitting candidate.changed and calling e.validate; no candidate-vs-plan comparison exists on that path. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] taskContext.Files are the paths the plan names; changedPaths(diff) omits deleted files, so the check reads report.FromDiff(diff).Files directly. (internal/workflow/engine.go) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] inspectTestEdits inspects only granted files and diffFileStates already classifies every changed path by status; neither compares the candidate to the plan. (internal/workflow/testedit.go) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: architectural-authority-granted\n"}
{"id":"20260829T003810.937443018Z-f4113f82","time":"2026-08-29T00:38:10.937443018Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"system","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Supplied plan (not architect-produced; sha256 45d8b6c7f6ed7f89d8be4bf4a07c094916f2042dcd06cdd807d6b586ec3471df)\nA candidate is confined to the files its plan names: after the worker's diff is read and before validation, audit, review or admission, every changed path -- added, modified, deleted or renamed -- must be one the plan named; any other path refuses the candidate, and no test-edit grant enlarges the named set.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Add the confinement check function in internal/workflow/testedit.go: input the diff and the plan's named files; output an error naming every path outside the plan, or nil.\n  2. Call it in runCandidate in internal/workflow/engine.go right after the ModeInspect refusal and before the candidate.changed event; return the error the way that refusal returns.\n  3. Add TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview, TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope and TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate to internal/workflow/engine_test.go, and TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening to internal/workflow/routine_test.go, building unified-diff strings in the tests.\n  4. Run gofmt -l cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./... .","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"A candidate is confined to the files its plan names: after the worker's diff is read and before validation, audit, review or admission, every changed path -- added, modified, deleted or renamed -- must be one the plan named; any other path refuses the candidate, and no test-edit grant enlarges the named set.","steps":["Add the confinement check function in internal/workflow/testedit.go: input the diff and the plan's named files; output an error naming every path outside the plan, or nil.","Call it in runCandidate in internal/workflow/engine.go right after the ModeInspect refusal and before the candidate.changed event; return the error the way that refusal returns.","Add TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview, TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope and TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate to internal/workflow/engine_test.go, and TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening to internal/workflow/routine_test.go, building unified-diff strings in the tests.","Run gofmt -l cmd internal, go vet ./..., and go test ./... ."],"consequences":"A worker that touches a path the plan did not name no longer reaches validation, audit, review or admission; the plan must be revised and the run repeated. Candidates within their plan behave exactly as before.","files":["internal/workflow/engine.go","internal/workflow/testedit.go","internal/workflow/engine_test.go","internal/workflow/routine_test.go"],"mode":"modify","plan":"In runCandidate (internal/workflow/engine.go), immediately after the read-only (ModeInspect) refusal and before the candidate.changed event and e.validate, refuse a candidate whose diff touches any path the plan did not name: the paths come from report.FromDiff(diff).Files (every status, deletions and renames included), the named set is tc.Files canonicalised with path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f)) exactly as architecturalFiles does, and the refusal error names every path outside the plan and the plan's named files. Put the check in one function beside inspectTestEdits and diffFileStates in internal/workflow/testedit.go, taking the diff and the named files only -- it must not take or read test-edit grants, so a grant cannot enlarge the set. The refusal returns from runCandidate the way the ModeInspect refusal does, so nothing downstream (validation, audit, Level-1 classification, review, admission) sees a wider candidate; the candidate worktree is left as it is. Tests in internal/workflow/engine_test.go: TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview (a diff touching one path outside the plan is refused, naming that path; a diff touching only named paths passes; a deletion outside the plan is refused), TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope (the check has no grant input, and a test file that would be grantable but is not named is refused), TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate (a candidate wider than a supplied plan is refused and the supplied plan's Digest and Files are unchanged). Test in internal/workflow/routine_test.go: TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening (a diff touching internal/workflow/routine.go plus one unnamed path is refused by this check, which does not depend on any Level-1 classification). No other behaviour changes; no signature changes; no new files.","claims":[{"statement":"runCandidate refuses a read-only plan whose candidate changed files immediately before emitting candidate.changed and calling e.validate; no candidate-vs-plan comparison exists on that path.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"taskContext.Files are the paths the plan names; changedPaths(diff) omits deleted files, so the check reads report.FromDiff(diff).Files directly.","about":"internal/workflow/engine.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"inspectTestEdits inspects only granted files and diffFileStates already classifies every changed path by status; neither compares the candidate to the plan.","about":"internal/workflow/testedit.go","source":"repository"}],"plan_source":"supplied","plan_digest":"45d8b6c7f6ed7f89d8be4bf4a07c094916f2042dcd06cdd807d6b586ec3471df"}}
