{"id":"20260829T004319.877704493Z-a60818f3","time":"2026-08-29T00:43:19.877704493Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW7UWK5Smccr3upJkC8V\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01Nh9nBxGkLnxL2fhr7U4bnx\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git add -A \u0026\u0026 git commit -q -F - \u003c\u003c'EOF' \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline -1\\nfeat(workflow): a candidate is confined to the files its plan names\\n\\nAfter the worker's diff is read and before anything downstream sees it,\\nevery changed path -- added, modified, deleted, or either side of a\\nrename -- must be one the plan named, or the candidate is refused.\\n\\nThe plan's file list bounded what the worker was ASKED to change and\\nnothing read it again afterwards: a candidate that also touched a file\\noutside the plan reached validation, the audit, the Level-1\\nclassification, the reviewer and admission as though the plan had named\\nit. The Level-1 classifier does hold such a condition, but it stops at\\nthe first categorical exclusion, so a candidate touching the governance\\npath is reported as touching the governance path and its widening is\\nnever mentioned -- and the classifier grants nothing anyway.\\n\\nconfineToPlannedFiles takes the diff and the plan's files and nothing\\nelse. In particular it takes no test-edit grant: a grant is authority to\\nedit a file the plan already names, never authority to touch one it does\\nnot, and a check that could read grants would be a check a grant could\\nwiden.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\\nEOF\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1604,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":101503,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1604},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"48a09178-a065-4f81-877c-dd60a4e7bbac\",\"uuid\":\"f21e7eec-b0c6-43b3-aa95-055a2600a2f9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:43:19.874Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW7UVWi1JbZX5kndefuv\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260829T004319.897488520Z-47f80e56","time":"2026-08-29T00:43:19.89748852Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\",\"rate_limit_info\":{\"status\":\"allowed\",\"resetsAt\":1787971200,\"rateLimitType\":\"five_hour\",\"overageStatus\":\"rejected\",\"overageDisabledReason\":\"org_level_disabled\",\"isUsingOverage\":false,\"unifiedWindows\":{\"five_hour\":{\"utilization\":0.46,\"resetsAt\":1787971200},\"seven_day\":{\"utilization\":0.49,\"resetsAt\":1788397200}}},\"uuid\":\"b704b669-87ce-49d4-b64e-c34a2fa76979\",\"session_id\":\"48a09178-a065-4f81-877c-dd60a4e7bbac\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260829T004320.106301435Z-383597ca","time":"2026-08-29T00:43:20.106301435Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Nh9nBxGkLnxL2fhr7U4bnx\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"c2ae239 feat(workflow): a candidate is confined to the files its plan names\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"48a09178-a065-4f81-877c-dd60a4e7bbac\",\"uuid\":\"39d55844-25a1-4157-94bf-43f0332d4a2d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:43:20.105Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"c2ae239 feat(workflow): a candidate is confined to the files its plan names\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false}}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260829T004340.061276360Z-4023a231","time":"2026-08-29T00:43:40.06127636Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW7VbuTbYbxj9ChKYa5F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Implemented the bounded plan; nothing beyond it.\\n\\n**What changed** (4 files, +258, no deletions, no signature changes, no new files):\\n\\n1. `internal/workflow/testedit.go:238` — `confineToPlannedFiles(diff string, planned []string) error`, beside `inspectTestEdits`/`diffFileStates`. Reads paths through `report.FromDiff(diff).Files` (every status; both sides of a rename), canonicalises the named set with `path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f))` exactly as `architecturalFiles` does, and returns an error naming every path outside the plan and the plan's named files. It takes the diff and the named files only — no grant input, so no grant can enlarge the set. A small `plannedOrNone` helper keeps a plan that named nothing from rendering as blank.\\n\\n2. `internal/workflow/engine.go:1250` — called in `runCandidate` immediately after the `ModeInspect` refusal and before the `candidate.changed` event, returning `(false, plan, lastReview, lastAudit, err)` the way that refusal does. Validation, audit, Level-1 classification, review and admission are all downstream of it; the worktree is untouched.\\n\\n3. `internal/workflow/engine_test.go` — `TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview` (unnamed path refused by name, named-only diff passes including the plan's `./` spelling, deletion outside the plan refused, rename out of the plan refused, plus source-order assertions that the check sits after the read-only refusal and before the event/validate/audit/classify), `TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope` (real grant fixture from `testedit_test.go`, grantable-but-unnamed test file refused, exact signature and call site asserted, body reads no grant identifier), `TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate` (refusal leaves `PlanDigest`, `Files` and `PlanSource` unchanged). Three small unified-diff builders (`unifiedModify`/`unifiedDelete`/`unifiedRename`).\\n\\n4. `internal/workflow/routine_test.go` — `TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening`: `classifyRoutine` blocks on the governance path and never mentions the unnamed `internal/tui/model.go`; the check refuses it by name and its body consults no classifier symbol.\\n\\n**Verification**\\n- `gofmt -l cmd internal`: clean. `go vet ./...`: clean.\\n- `go test ./...`: all packages pass except `internal/publish` — `TestCommitAndPushReachARealRemote` fails with `sensei-code: push is refused; publication is human-owned and the push capability is not granted`. That is this worker session's capability guard refusing a push, not my change (no file under `internal/publish` is touched); it is the sibling of the recorded `TestGuardActuallyRefusesAPush` worker-session failure.\\n- Mutation-checked: stubbing `confineToPlannedFiles` to return `nil` fails all four tests; removing the call site fails two.\\n\\n**Consequence worth the architect's attention (not something I changed on my own):** applied to a plan whose `Files` list is empty, the rule refuses every candidate — an empty named set names nothing. That is the fail-closed reading of the stated intent and the error says `the plan names: (no file)`, but nothing upstream requires a `ModeModify` plan to name a file, so a plan that omits `files` now ends the run instead of proceeding. I left this as the plan specifies rather than adding an empty-set exemption.\\n\\nI did not run `sensei propose`: recording a scar would stage edits to `docs/awareness/*.yaml`, which the plan does not name.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/testedit.go) | invariants: workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope, workflow.repeated_resume_cannot_mint_authority | uncertainty: a plan with an empty file list now refuses every candidate — stated above, not decided around.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1069,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":103107,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1069},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"48a09178-a065-4f81-877c-dd60a4e7bbac\",\"uuid\":\"f5e745d1-ae73-45b6-87c6-051dfb70e962\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:43:40.042Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW7Vb2sWqFMGn6wcNh6U\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
