{"id":"20260829T005211.044058967Z-e13dd3a8","time":"2026-08-29T00:52:11.044058967Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW8ASr5w5A17o9jyejPk\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01ULmNSjTX4kMntfvXjmYp7T\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git show --stat fdd5b1d \u0026\u0026 echo \\\"=====FULL=====\\\" \u0026\u0026 git show fdd5b1d\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":827,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":30297,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":827},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"752e2b95-05cd-40e0-a81d-2e202234604f\",\"uuid\":\"5a7a4e23-ff91-4db0-9811-95b6cf20ac63\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:52:11.041Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW8AS8vN4VyLAZX5Yv3Y\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
{"id":"20260829T005211.091264684Z-18e5fcf6","time":"2026-08-29T00:52:11.091264684Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01ULmNSjTX4kMntfvXjmYp7T\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"commit fdd5b1d7b9832729caf3c486ccf03eda550f8808\\nAuthor: davecourtois \u003cdave.courtois60@gmail.com\u003e\\nDate:   Fri Aug 28 20:49:58 2026 -0400\\n\\n    fix(workflow): the candidate that is reviewed is the one that is confined -- validation re-reads the diff after a mutating formatter, so the same bound is applied again\\n    \\n    The pre-validation check bounded what the WORKER produced. e.validate then\\n    runs the configured formatters against the candidate worktree and re-reads\\n    the diff, deliberately, because evidence gathered before a rewrite is\\n    evidence about different bytes. Everything downstream consumes that re-read\\n    diff.\\n    \\n    A formatter is a configured command with write access to the whole\\n    worktree. It can create or rewrite a path the plan never named, and that\\n    path then reached the validation evidence, the prospective and test-edit\\n    inspections, the audit, the Level-1 classification, the reviewer and\\n    admission unrefused -- past the only check that reads the plan. Placement\\n    before validation proved placement, not confinement of the candidate\\n    actually reviewed.\\n    \\n    confineToPlannedFiles is therefore called a second time, on the diff\\n    e.validate returns, before ValidationRun is emitted and before any\\n    inspection, audit, classification, review or admission reads it. The\\n    pre-validation check stays: it names the worker as the author of a widening\\n    the worker committed, which a single post-validation check would blame on\\n    the formatter.\\n    \\n    TestAFormatterCannotWidenTheCandidateAfterValidation runs the real path --\\n    a real repository, a worker edit inside the plan that the first check\\n    passes, e.validate with a formatter that writes an unplanned file, and the\\n    diff validation actually returns, which is refused by name.\\n    \\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\\n\\n internal/workflow/engine.go      |  14 +++++\\n internal/workflow/engine_test.go | 117 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n 2 files changed, 131 insertions(+)\\n=====FULL=====\\ncommit fdd5b1d7b9832729caf3c486ccf03eda550f8808\\nAuthor: davecourtois \u003cdave.courtois60@gmail.com\u003e\\nDate:   Fri Aug 28 20:49:58 2026 -0400\\n\\n    fix(workflow): the candidate that is reviewed is the one that is confined -- validation re-reads the diff after a mutating formatter, so the same bound is applied again\\n    \\n    The pre-validation check bounded what the WORKER produced. e.validate then\\n    runs the configured formatters against the candidate worktree and re-reads\\n    the diff, deliberately, because evidence gathered before a rewrite is\\n    evidence about different bytes. Everything downstream consumes that re-read\\n    diff.\\n    \\n    A formatter is a configured command with write access to the whole\\n    worktree. It can create or rewrite a path the plan never named, and that\\n    path then reached the validation evidence, the prospective and test-edit\\n    inspections, the audit, the Level-1 classification, the reviewer and\\n    admission unrefused -- past the only check that reads the plan. Placement\\n    before validation proved placement, not confinement of the candidate\\n    actually reviewed.\\n    \\n    confineToPlannedFiles is therefore called a second time, on the diff\\n    e.validate returns, before ValidationRun is emitted and before any\\n    inspection, audit, classification, review or admission reads it. The\\n    pre-validation check stays: it names the worker as the author of a widening\\n    the worker committed, which a single post-validation check would blame on\\n    the formatter.\\n    \\n    TestAFormatterCannotWidenTheCandidateAfterValidation runs the real path --\\n    a real repository, a worker edit inside the plan that the first check\\n    passes, e.validate with a formatter that writes an unplanned file, and the\\n    diff validation actually returns, which is refused by name.\\n    \\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\\n\\ndiff --git a/internal/workflow/engine.go b/internal/workflow/engine.go\\nindex 983406b..7eaf210 100644\\n--- a/internal/workflow/engine.go\\n+++ b/internal/workflow/engine.go\\n@@ -1273,6 +1273,20 @@ func (e *Engine) runCandidate(ctx context.Context, sc *sensei.Client, start cert\\n \\t\\tif err != nil {\\n \\t\\t\\treturn false, plan, lastReview, lastAudit, err\\n \\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\t// And again, on the diff validation returned. The check above bounded\\n+\\t\\t// what the WORKER produced; validation then ran a mutating formatter\\n+\\t\\t// against the candidate worktree and re-read the diff, so the bytes\\n+\\t\\t// everything downstream consumes are not the bytes that were confined.\\n+\\t\\t// A formatter is a configured command with write access to the whole\\n+\\t\\t// worktree: it can create or rewrite a path the plan never named, and\\n+\\t\\t// that path would otherwise reach the validation evidence, the\\n+\\t\\t// prospective and test-edit inspections, the audit, the Level-1\\n+\\t\\t// classification, the reviewer and admission unrefused. The candidate\\n+\\t\\t// that is actually reviewed is the one that must be confined, so the\\n+\\t\\t// same bound is applied to it, before any of them has read it.\\n+\\t\\tif err := confineToPlannedFiles(diff, tc.Files); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\t\\treturn false, plan, lastReview, lastAudit, err\\n+\\t\\t}\\n \\t\\te.emit(event.New(e.SessionID, taskID, event.SourceSystem, event.ValidationRun, evidence.Render(), evidence))\\n \\n \\t\\t// Post-creation inspection of every declared prospective surface\\ndiff --git a/internal/workflow/engine_test.go b/internal/workflow/engine_test.go\\nindex 286c11d..41de985 100644\\n--- a/internal/workflow/engine_test.go\\n+++ b/internal/workflow/engine_test.go\\n@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ import (\\n \\t\\\"go/parser\\\"\\n \\t\\\"go/token\\\"\\n \\t\\\"os\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"os/exec\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"path/filepath\\\"\\n \\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n \\t\\\"testing\\\"\\n \\t\\\"time\\\"\\n@@ -16,9 +18,13 @@ import (\\n \\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/roles\\\"\\n \\n \\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/authority\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/broker\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/config\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/decision\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/event\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/gitx\\\"\\n \\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/taskstate\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/globulario/sensei-code/internal/validation\\\"\\n )\\n \\n func TestDecodeModelJSON(t *testing.T) {\\n@@ -1467,3 +1473,114 @@ func TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate(t *testing.T) {\\n \\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"the plan stopped being supplied: %q\\\", tc.PlanSource)\\n \\t}\\n }\\n+\\n+// The confinement check above bounds what the WORKER produced. Validation then\\n+// runs a mutating formatter against the candidate worktree and re-reads the\\n+// diff, and the bytes everything downstream consumes are those. A formatter is\\n+// a configured command with write access to the whole worktree, so it can add\\n+// or rewrite a path the plan never named -- after the only check that reads the\\n+// plan has already passed.\\n+//\\n+// This runs the real path: a real repository, a real worker edit inside the\\n+// plan, e.validate with a configured formatter that creates an unplanned file,\\n+// and the diff validation actually returns.\\n+func TestAFormatterCannotWidenTheCandidateAfterValidation(t *testing.T) {\\n+\\troot := t.TempDir()\\n+\\tgit := func(args ...string) string {\\n+\\t\\tt.Helper()\\n+\\t\\tcmd := exec.Command(\\\"git\\\", append([]string{\\\"-C\\\", root}, args...)...)\\n+\\t\\tcmd.Env = append(os.Environ(), \\\"GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=t\\\", \\\"GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=t@t\\\", \\\"GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=t\\\", \\\"GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=t@t\\\")\\n+\\t\\tout, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\\n+\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"git %v: %v\\\\n%s\\\", args, err, out)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\\n+\\t}\\n+\\twrite := func(rel, body string) {\\n+\\t\\tt.Helper()\\n+\\t\\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(root, rel), []byte(body), 0o644); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\t\\tt.Fatal(err)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tgit(\\\"init\\\", \\\"-q\\\")\\n+\\twrite(\\\"planned.go\\\", \\\"package p\\\\n\\\\nvar A = 1\\\\n\\\")\\n+\\tgit(\\\"add\\\", \\\".\\\")\\n+\\tgit(\\\"commit\\\", \\\"-q\\\", \\\"-m\\\", \\\"base\\\")\\n+\\tbase := git(\\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\")\\n+\\n+\\t// The worker changes exactly the file the plan named.\\n+\\tplanned := []string{\\\"planned.go\\\"}\\n+\\twrite(\\\"planned.go\\\", \\\"package p\\\\n\\\\nvar A = 2\\\\n\\\")\\n+\\n+\\tctx := context.Background()\\n+\\trepo := gitx.Repo{Root: root}\\n+\\tdiff, err := repo.CandidateDiff(ctx, base)\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatal(err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif err := confineToPlannedFiles(diff, planned); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"the worker's own candidate stayed inside the plan and was refused: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\n+\\t// The configured formatter writes a file nobody planned.\\n+\\te := \u0026Engine{Repo: repo}\\n+\\te.Config.Permissions.RunFormatters = true\\n+\\te.Config.Validation.Format = []config.Command{{Command: \\\"sh\\\", Args: []string{\\\"-c\\\", \\\"printf 'package p\\\\\\\\n' \u003e generated.go\\\"}}}\\n+\\tevidence, after, err := e.validate(ctx, \\\"task-1\\\", base, broker.New(e.Config.Permissions), repo, diff)\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"validation errored rather than returning the rewritten candidate: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif !strings.Contains(after, \\\"generated.go\\\") {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"the formatter did not widen the re-read diff, so this test no longer exercises the case:\\\\n%s\\\", after)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\t// Validation itself is content with it: the formatter exited zero and\\n+\\t// nothing in the bundle is about scope. Refusing here is this check's job.\\n+\\tfor _, c := range evidence.Checks {\\n+\\t\\tif c.Outcome == validation.Failed {\\n+\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"the fixture's formatter failed, which is not the case under test: %s\\\", c.Detail)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\n+\\terr = confineToPlannedFiles(after, planned)\\n+\\tif err == nil {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"a formatter added a file the plan never named and the candidate was not refused\\\")\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \\\"generated.go\\\") {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"the refusal does not name the path the formatter added: %v\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\n+\\t// And the refusal happens where nothing has yet consumed the widened\\n+\\t// candidate: after validation returns, before its evidence is emitted and\\n+\\t// before the prospective and test-edit inspections, the audit, the Level-1\\n+\\t// classification, the review and admission read that diff.\\n+\\tsrc := rawSource(t, \\\"internal/workflow/engine.go\\\")\\n+\\tcall := \\\"confineToPlannedFiles(diff, tc.Files)\\\"\\n+\\tvalidated := strings.Index(src, \\\"e.validate(ctx\\\")\\n+\\tfirst := strings.Index(src, call)\\n+\\tif validated \u003c 0 || first \u003c 0 || first \u003e validated {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"the candidate loop no longer confines the worker's diff before validation\\\")\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tsecond := strings.Index(src[validated:], call)\\n+\\tif second \u003c 0 {\\n+\\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"the diff validation returns is never confined; only the worker's own diff is\\\")\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tsecond += validated\\n+\\tfor _, downstream := range []struct {\\n+\\t\\tat   int\\n+\\t\\twhat string\\n+\\t}{\\n+\\t\\t{strings.Index(src, \\\"event.ValidationRun\\\"), \\\"the validation evidence\\\"},\\n+\\t\\t{strings.Index(src, \\\"inspectProspectiveSurfaces(\\\"), \\\"the prospective inspection\\\"},\\n+\\t\\t{strings.Index(src, \\\"inspectTestEdits(\\\"), \\\"the test-edit inspection\\\"},\\n+\\t\\t{strings.Index(src, `sc.CallTool(\\\"awareness_audit_diff\\\"`), \\\"the audit\\\"},\\n+\\t\\t{strings.Index(src, \\\"e.classifyForDarkRun(\\\"), \\\"the Level-1 classification\\\"},\\n+\\t\\t{strings.Index(src, \\\"reviewPacket(\\\"), \\\"the review\\\"},\\n+\\t} {\\n+\\t\\tif downstream.at \u003c 0 {\\n+\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"the candidate loop no longer reaches %s\\\", downstream.what)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\tif second \u003e downstream.at {\\n+\\t\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"a candidate widened by the formatter reaches %s before it is refused\\\", downstream.what)\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t}\\n+}\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"752e2b95-05cd-40e0-a81d-2e202234604f\",\"uuid\":\"6be404af-5bad-4f5b-b2d9-d84d72f70507\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:52:11.090Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"commit fdd5b1d7b9832729caf3c486ccf03eda550f8808\\nAuthor: davecourtois \u003cdave.courtois60@gmail.com\u003e\\nDate:   Fri Aug 28 20:49:58 2026 -0400\\n\\n    fix(workflow): the candidate that is reviewed is the one that is confined -- validation re-reads the diff after a mutating formatter, so the same bound is applied again\\n    \\n    The pre-validation check bounded what the WORKER produced. e.validate then\\n    runs the configured formatters against the candidate worktree and re-reads\\n    the diff, deliberately, because evidence gathered before a rewrite is\\n    evidence about different bytes. Everything downstream consumes that re-read\\n    diff.\\n    \\n    A formatter is a configured command with write access to the whole\\n    worktree. It can