{"id":"20260829T005307.653610190Z-739d3676","time":"2026-08-29T00:53:07.65361019Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW8Dv14FoU122CQvE7XZ\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_013HNnLnPn77XfuoBTwV9sSG\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd \\\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\\\" \u0026\u0026 git commit -q -F - \u003c\u003c'EOF' \u0026\u0026 git log --oneline -3\\nfix(workflow): the confinement check is only the one the plan authorized\\n\\nReview finding f1 (blocking): the candidate had added a second\\nconfineToPlannedFiles call after e.validate returns, plus\\nTestAFormatterCannotWidenTheCandidateAfterValidation and the imports that\\ntest alone needed.\\n\\nThe supplied plan places one check -- immediately after the ModeInspect\\nrefusal, before the candidate.changed event and e.validate -- and says\\nexpressly \\\"No other behaviour changes\\\". A second refusal after validation\\nhas executed and before ValidationRun is emitted is a new workflow\\nbehaviour and a new refusal path, and it was not in the authorized\\ntransition or the requested test set. A worker that widens its own plan\\nbecause it judged the wider bound better is the failure this very feature\\nexists to refuse.\\n\\nfdd5b1d is therefore reverted in full. What remains is exactly what the\\nplan named: one check in confineToPlannedFiles, called once in\\nrunCandidate after the read-only refusal, and the four specified tests.\\n\\nThe gap that commit described is real and is left open deliberately: a\\nconfigured formatter has write access to the whole candidate worktree and\\ne.validate re-reads the diff, so a formatter-written path is not confined.\\nClosing it needs a revised architectural plan that authorizes the\\npost-validation refusal and its proof; it is not the worker's to decide.\\n\\ngofmt -l cmd internal clean; go vet ./... clean; go test ./... all pass.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\\nEOF\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2308,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":43464,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2308},\"output_tokens\":2,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"752e2b95-05cd-40e0-a81d-2e202234604f\",\"uuid\":\"49149c1f-7b81-4f59-9774-c03085c1b558\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:53:07.650Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW8DuAT8CaSz5mz69hbB\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
