{"id":"20260829T005323.626565617Z-2daa3fbe","time":"2026-08-29T00:53:23.626565617Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW8F9e8EDq4zLWEnxR1F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Reconciled review finding f1. Commit `be3cdbe` reverts `fdd5b1d` in full.\\n\\n**What changed**\\n- Removed the second `confineToPlannedFiles(diff, tc.Files)` call after `e.validate` in `internal/workflow/engine.go:1273`.\\n- Removed `TestAFormatterCannotWidenTheCandidateAfterValidation` from `internal/workflow/engine_test.go`, along with the imports it alone required (`os/exec`, `path/filepath`, `internal/broker`, `internal/config`, `internal/gitx`, `internal/validation`).\\n\\n**What remains** is exactly the plan's shape — net diff against `f01592b` is +258 lines, no deletions:\\n- `internal/workflow/testedit.go`: `confineToPlannedFiles(diff string, planned []string) error`, beside `inspectTestEdits`/`diffFileStates`, taking no grant input.\\n- `internal/workflow/engine.go:1251`: one call, immediately after the `ModeInspect` refusal and before the `candidate.changed` event, returning the way that refusal returns.\\n- The four specified tests: `TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview`, `TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope`, `TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate` (engine_test.go), `TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening` (routine_test.go). All pass.\\n\\n**Verification**: `gofmt -l cmd internal` clean, `go vet ./...` clean, `go test ./...` all packages ok.\\n\\n**Left undone, deliberately, for the architect**: the gap `fdd5b1d` described is real. `e.validate` runs configured formatters with write access to the whole candidate worktree and then re-reads the diff; everything downstream (validation evidence, prospective/test-edit inspection, audit, Level-1 classification, review, admission) consumes that re-read diff, which the single pre-validation check has not bounded. A formatter-written path is therefore not confined today. Per the review instruction, closing it needs a revised architectural plan that explicitly authorizes a post-validation refusal and its proof — I have not decided that for you. Briefing on `internal/workflow/engine.go` lists no forbidden fix or required test bearing on either the removal or that gap.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope, sensei_code.authority.only_an_explicit_answer_satisfies_a_boundary | uncertainty: a formatter can still widen the candidate after validation re-reads the diff; unrefused until a revised plan authorizes the second check\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":883,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":46823,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":883},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"752e2b95-05cd-40e0-a81d-2e202234604f\",\"uuid\":\"da085778-1391-4057-a8eb-4b0fd7145ca9\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:53:23.615Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW8F8iJtuPDaTQod7xpX\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
