{"id":"20260829T005340.402186271Z-3ab89987","time":"2026-08-29T00:53:40.402186271Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"reviewer","kind":"output","summary":"In runCandidate (internal/workflow/engine.go), immediately after the read-only (ModeInspect) refusal and before the candidate.changed event and e.validate, refuse a candidate whose diff touches any path the plan did not name: the paths come from report.FromDiff(diff).Files (every status, deletions and renames included), the named set is tc.Files canonicalised with path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f)) exactly as architecturalFiles does, and the refusal error names every path outside the plan and the plan's named files. Put the check in one function beside inspectTestEdits and diffFileStates in internal/workflow/testedit.go, taking the diff and the named files only -- it must not take or read test-edit grants, so a grant cannot enlarge the set. The refusal returns from runCandidate the way the ModeInspect refusal does, so nothing downstream (validation, audit, Level-1 classification, review, admission) sees a wider candidate; the candidate worktree is left as it is. Tests in internal/workflow/engine_test.go: TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview (a diff touching one path outside the plan is refused, naming that path; a diff touching only named paths passes; a deletion outside the plan is refused), TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope (the check has no grant input, and a test file that would be grantable but is not named is refused), TestASuppliedPlanIsNotWidenedByTheCandidate (a candidate wider than a supplied plan is refused and the supplied plan's Digest and Files are unchanged). Test in internal/workflow/routine_test.go: TestGovernancePathClassificationCannotMaskScopeWidening (a diff touching internal/workflow/routine.go plus one unnamed path is refused by this check, which does not depend on any Level-1 classification). No other behaviour changes; no signature changes; no new files.","payload":{"stream":"stderr"}}
