{"id":"20260829T010403.088568483Z-8d2e5027","time":"2026-08-29T01:04:03.088568483Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"reviewer","kind":"review.completed","summary":"ESCALATE: The check itself is faithful to the supplied plan — it takes only the diff and tc.Files, canonicalises like architecturalFiles, reads both sides of a rename, and sits between the ModeInspect refusal and the candidate.changed event — and gofmt/vet/build/test all passed on this exact revision. But the plan pins the confined set to tc.Files, and tc.Files is written once (engine.go:707) and never updated when a reviewer escalation makes the architect re-plan, while routing, coverage, test-edit grants and prospective grants ARE recomputed from the revised decision's Files (engine.go:1669/1789/1919 → 2197 → 2570-2571). After such a revision the engine can hand the worker a grant for a file the confinement check will refuse, and the refusal is terminal. Which file list 'the plan' means after an architect revision is an authority question the worker cannot settle inside a plan that names tc.Files. Separately, the candidate's inline comment claims validation, audit, classification, review and admission 'see only a candidate that stayed inside its plan', which is false: e.validate re-reads the diff after 'gofmt -w cmd internal' (config.go:205, engine.go:4395-4402) and that wider re-read diff is what the audit, the classifier, the reviewer and publication consume. Sensei vouches for none of this — preflight is PREFLIGHT_STATUS_EMPTY / UNKNOWN_IMPACT with 'coverage: anchors=0 files=0 indexed=0 sufficient=false', and the diff audit's pass reports only 'No blocking findings found in supplied diff'.  (reviewer · via claude · session fresh · candidate a5eb383fb17a)","payload":{"provenance":{"task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","role":"reviewer","provider":"claude","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","session_mode":"fresh","base_sha":"f01592b0f0828605ed254047fc064f41dacc78f2","candidate_digest":"a5eb383fb17a8853","graph_build_commit":"fac399f8225f","at":"2026-08-29T01:04:03.088336341Z"},"decision":"escalate","summary":"The check itself is faithful to the supplied plan — it takes only the diff and tc.Files, canonicalises like architecturalFiles, reads both sides of a rename, and sits between the ModeInspect refusal and the candidate.changed event — and gofmt/vet/build/test all passed on this exact revision. But the plan pins the confined set to tc.Files, and tc.Files is written once (engine.go:707) and never updated when a reviewer escalation makes the architect re-plan, while routing, coverage, test-edit grants and prospective grants ARE recomputed from the revised decision's Files (engine.go:1669/1789/1919 → 2197 → 2570-2571). After such a revision the engine can hand the worker a grant for a file the confinement check will refuse, and the refusal is terminal. Which file list 'the plan' means after an architect revision is an authority question the worker cannot settle inside a plan that names tc.Files. Separately, the candidate's inline comment claims validation, audit, classification, review and admission 'see only a candidate that stayed inside its plan', which is false: e.validate re-reads the diff after 'gofmt -w cmd internal' (config.go:205, engine.go:4395-4402) and that wider re-read diff is what the audit, the classifier, the reviewer and publication consume. Sensei vouches for none of this — preflight is PREFLIGHT_STATUS_EMPTY / UNKNOWN_IMPACT with 'coverage: anchors=0 files=0 indexed=0 sufficient=false', and the diff audit's pass reports only 'No blocking findings found in supplied diff'.","instructions":"Architect decision needed on f1 before this lands: state whether a candidate is confined to the file list of the decision that was ROUTED (tc.Files, as the supplied plan says) or to the file list of the plan in force after a reviewer-escalated revision. If it is the routed list, then the escalation branch (engine.go:1523-1545) must not silently continue when the architect's revised decision names files outside tc.Files — that combination is an authorised plan the boundary will kill — and the worker should be told which refusal shape to use there. If it is the revised list, say so explicitly and say what re-establishes coverage for the newly named files, because binding to revised.Files lets a post-hoc revision enlarge the confined set for files whose per-file examination was proven under a different plan (the M25 §1 / PR #115 laundering shape). Do not resolve this by having confineToPlannedFiles read anything besides the diff and a file list.\n\nRegardless of that answer, the worker must repair f2 without changing behaviour: narrow the comment at engine.go (the new block above confineToPlannedFiles) and the doc comment in testedit.go so they claim only what the code proves — the WORKER'S diff is confined — and name the residual out loud: e.validate re-reads the diff after the mutating formatter and nothing re-checks that re-read, so a path the formatter introduces reaches the audit, the Level-1 classification, the reviewer, EvidenceSnapshot.ChangedPaths (engine.go:1389) and publication (engine.go:788 → publish.Open, which commits exactly those paths). Also fix f3 by adding the empty-plan case to TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview, and f4 by naming the divergence from notPlanned in the doc comment.","findings":[{"id":"f1","severity":"blocking","claim":"'A grant is computed from the plan's files and cannot reach outside them' (TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope), and more generally that tc.Files is the plan's named set for the whole candidate loop.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:1248 (the new call, confineToPlannedFiles(diff, tc.Files)); engine.go:707-731 (tc built once); engine.go:1523-1545 (reviewer-escalation branch: only `plan` is updated); engine.go:1669/1789/1919 → 2197 → 2570-2571 (routing, derivedCoverage, setTestEditGrants and setProspectiveGrants recomputed from the revised decision's Files)","reason":"tc.Files is assigned once from the FIRST architectureDecision and is never reassigned anywhere in the package (its only other read is CandidateCapture at engine.go:1144). On a reviewer escalation the change lane calls resolveArchitectureForRevision → resolveArchitecture → routePlan on the REVISED decision, which overwrites the task's routing, coverage anchors, test-edit grants and prospective grants from revised.Files, and sets `plan` to the revised prose, while tc.Files keeps the original list. The engine therefore holds two answers to 'which files does this plan name': the one that issues authority, and the one this new check enforces. Before this candidate the divergence only affected the dark-run classifier, which records and blocks nothing; now it terminates the task. The candidate's own test asserts the impossibility of exactly this ('a grant is computed from the plan's files and cannot reach outside them'), which is true only for the first decision. Supplied plans are immune (errSuppliedPlanCannotBeRevised), so this is live precisely in the architect-authored lane.","correction":"Architect must fix the binding, not the worker guessing: either (a) confinement stays bound to the routed decision's files and the escalation branch refuses/re-routes when revised.Files differs, or (b) confinement follows the plan in force, with a stated mechanism that re-establishes per-file examination for the newly named files. Then pin the chosen answer with a test that drives a plan revision (or, at minimum, asserts the file list the check is given is the same one the recorded grants were computed from).","proof_gap":"No test exercises confineToPlannedFiles across a plan revision. TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope proves only that the function signature takes no grants and that its body mentions no grant identifier; it never shows that the list passed in is the list the engine's live grants were derived from."},{"id":"f2","severity":"major","claim":"'before anything downstream has read the candidate: validation, the audit, the Level-1 classification, the reviewer and admission all see only a candidate that stayed inside its plan, or they see none' (new comment at engine.go), and the testedit.go doc comment's 'nothing downstream ... is ever handed a wider change than the one that was planned'.","reference":"internal/workflow/engine.go:1248-1257 (comment) and internal/workflow/testedit.go (confineToPlannedFiles doc comment), against engine.go:4393-4402 (e.validate runs the mutating formatter and re-reads via repo.CandidateDiff) and internal/config/config.go:205 (default Format is `gofmt -w cmd internal`)","reason":"e.validate returns a NEW diff read after `gofmt -w cmd internal` has rewritten the candidate worktree; CandidateDiff → CandidateCapture(base, nil) re-runs `add --intent-to-add .` and diffs the whole tree, so any file the formatter rewrote — including one the plan never named, e.g. a file left unformatted at the base or reformatted by a newer gofmt — enters the diff AFTER the confinement check has already run. That post-validate diff is what the audit (engine.go:1328), classifyForDarkRun (1420), the reviewer, EvidenceSnapshot.ChangedPaths (1389) and publication (788 → publish.Open, which commits exactly those paths) all consume. The check is a real boundary on the worker's diff, which is what the architect intent asks for; the comment asserts a containment over validation, admission and publication that the code does not hold, and the ordering assertions in TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview (source-text index comparisons) are read as proving it.","correction":"Narrow both comments to what is proven — the worker's diff is confined — and state the residual explicitly: the diff is re-read after the mutating formatter and that re-read is not confined. Do not add a second check here; that is a behaviour change the supplied plan excludes, so name the residual for the architect instead of quietly closing it.","proof_gap":"Nothing in the candidate or the validation evidence tests the post-validate diff against the plan's files; the 'RefusedBeforeReview' test proves only textual ordering inside engine.go."},{"id":"f3","severity":"minor","claim":"plannedOrNone: 'A plan that names nothing authorizes nothing, and saying so is the answer.'","reference":"internal/workflow/testedit.go (plannedOrNone) and internal/workflow/engine.go:1248","reason":"With tc.Files empty, every changed path is outside the plan, so the first non-empty candidate ends the task with a terminal error. Nothing upstream requires a non-empty file list for a modify plan — authority.go:414 raises the coverage gap only `if coverageAbsent \u0026\u0026 len(action.Files) != 0`, and coverageAtWorld simply returns false for an empty list — so an architect decision with no `files` reaches runCandidate today and previously proceeded to validation and review. The fail-closed reading is defensible, but it is a new terminal behaviour introduced by this candidate and the plan said 'no other behaviour changes', with no test pinning it.","correction":"Add the empty-plan case to TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview (a plan naming no file refuses any changed path, and the refusal says the plan names '(no file)'), so the intended fail-closed reading is evidence rather than a comment.","proof_gap":"No test covers planned == nil / empty, which is the one input where this check refuses everything."},{"id":"f4","severity":"minor","claim":"The new function is the repository's answer to 'which changed paths did the plan not name'.","reference":"internal/workflow/testedit.go (confineToPlannedFiles) vs internal/workflow/routine.go:290-303 (notPlanned, used by classifyRoutine step 8 at routine.go:256)","reason":"Two representations of the same predicate now disagree. notPlanned compares raw TrimSpace strings over shape.Paths() (b-side only); confineToPlannedFiles compares path.Clean'd strings over both sides of a rename. A plan spelling './internal/x.go' with a diff spelling 'internal/x.go' is inside the plan for the confinement check and 'touched files the plan did not name' for the classifier; a rename out of the plan is refused by one and invisible to the other. The candidate's routine_test.go acknowledges notPlanned by forbidding it in the body, so the divergence was seen and left unstated.","correction":"State the divergence in confineToPlannedFiles' doc comment (which spelling each side accepts and why the classifier's is not reused), or unify them under an architect decision — unifying is outside this plan's bound and must not be done silently.","proof_gap":"No test compares the two predicates on the same input, so nothing detects them drifting further apart."}]}}
